      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like a lot of shader code, but it\u0027s actually not that bad. (There\u0027s probably a tighter form with fewer branches, but I\u0027m not worried about that yet). I know you\u0027re not real worried about it, but I have to ask: Should this be orthogonal to color space? From an API standpoint, it sure seems like it - but I realize that it makes the implementation much trickier (if I pick LinearSrgb + GamutMap, we need to interpolate, then transform, gamut map, transform...). Given that, I\u0027d be okay with this implementation, but that ultimately hinges on others agreeing with the strategy for CSS.",
      "revId": "a6745c70ac369505d6feaad6fe3a386b5b270ca1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
