      "writtenOn": "2024-01-02T18:42:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I suspect that there is a tighter form we can use, and we can probably move the constants into a separate uniform buffer.\n\nFor the API ... it depends on how this lands. If we end up saying that gamut mapping is intrinsic to `oklab` and `oklch` spaces (and only those spaces), then I think we end up just deleting the existing non-gamut-mapped versions. Personally I think that would be the most coherent scheme to go with (because I want these colors gamut mapped also when they\u0027re just specified as CSS literals).",
      "parentUuid": "1fc4b619_c9362530",
